pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: the same unguarded degree bookkeeping in `GeneralPBConstraint::add` at
% the i128 instantiation. The degree sum is i128::MIN + 3, the merge of `5 x1` with `5 ~x1`
% cancels 5, so the true degree is i128::MIN - 2 and used to wrap positive. The formula is
% satisfiable: the only constraint is trivially true.
f 1 ;
pol 1 ~x1 5 * + ;
pol 2 x2 w ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
